# Overview

This project provides credit information for our customers.
Currently, we have credit ML models called Vader, Anakin, and Obi-Wan.
Basically, These models predict credit scores based on customers' daily bank account balances, though the obi-wan requires additional parameters from API input.
The project scope covers everything from building daily balances to providing model scores for our company's finance services.

# Development guide

We primarily use Python for development.
The project will be deployed on the MLOps platform built on databricks in AWS.

Please also refer to databricks/README.

# Project Structure

The project is organized as follows:
- `aws/lambda`: Contains the lambda functions for external API
- `databricks/`: Contains Databricks notebooks for data processing and model execution
- `view_models/`: Contains data mart SQLs for the data pipeline

Please also refer to .cursor/rules/directory-layouts.mdc
